            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "MaxKare describes itself as an ecommerce retailer of home comfort, massage, heated and baby-care products, and its treadmills are sold under its name. The brand does not name a manufacturer or parent company, and we could not confirm one. Like most marketplace brands, the machines are made by contract manufacturers and sold mainly through Walmart.com.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "Where can I buy a MaxKare treadmill?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "Mainly on Walmart.com, where most MaxKare treadmills are listed, and on the brand’s own store at maxkare.net. We found no MaxKare treadmill in Amazon’s US product data on 14 October 2026. On Walmart, check whether Walmart or a marketplace seller is selling the unit, because that decides who handles returns.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "Is the MaxKare 3.5 HP treadmill good for running?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "Not for most people. It lists a 12 mph top speed, but its running surface is listed at 20 by 48 inches, and 48 inches is a walking length. Most adults need 55 inches or more to jog comfortably and about 60 to run. The 3.5 HP figure is not a continuous rating, so it cannot be compared with CHP figures on other brands.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "What is the weight limit on a MaxKare treadmill?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
